# Extra sensitive-path patterns for {{PROJECT_NAME}} — ENFORCED by the
# gaffer guardrail (hooks/guard.sh loads this file at runtime and appends
# these to its built-in SENSITIVE_PATH_PATTERNS). Mirror the "Sensitive paths"
# you list in .agents/domain-rules.md here so writes to them are actually blocked
# — both via the Edit/Write tools and via shell writes (cat >, sed -i, cp, tee).
#
# Format: one POSIX extended-regex (grep -E, case-insensitive) per line, matched
# against the target file path. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. A match
# DENIES the write (exit 2) until a human approves it.
#
# The plugin covers only GENERIC risk — auth/authz, secrets/.env/credentials,
# CI/deploy config, and cert/key files. It does NOT cover domain risk. Add THIS
# repo's domain-critical paths here (e.g. money movement for a financial app).
#
# Scope patterns to real MODULE paths, not bare keywords — a rule on the word
# "transfer" or "balance" false-positives on a load balancer or a DTO. Anchor to a
# directory or namespace you actually own.
#
# Examples (uncomment / adapt to this repo):
# (^|/)src/(payments|ledger|banking)/            # financial app: money movement
# (^|/)src/[^/]*/(pricing|billing|invoicing)/
# (^|/)core/(compliance|audit)/
# tenant[^/]*\.(cs|ts|py|go)$
